      "description": "The overview page must render the event settings navigation for this specific event, linking its sibling settings surfaces (landing preview, registration form, custom domain, automations). Catches a page that renders standalone instead of through the shared shell that carries the tab strip."
    },
    {
      "method": "event_overview_action_visibility_follows_the_shared_event_action_model",
      "severity": "S2",
      "description": "Expected visibility is read from the existing EventActionAvailability model, then compared against the rendered page: the metadata edit surface is offered on a DRAFT event and withheld on a PUBLISHED one. Catches a page that does not pass action availability into the shell (defaults leak every action) or that re-implements visibility with per-page conditionals."
    },
    {
      "method": "event_overview_exposes_no_state_changing_control_for_the_event",
      "severity": "S2",
      "description": "The read-only overview must expose no form submitting for this event, no mutating events-module form, no component form submission, and no publish/cancel/suspend/reactivate/force-end control. Catches the shell being adopted by copying the preview page's action row wholesale, quietly widening the read-only page into a state-changing one."
    },
    {
      "method": "landing_preview_keeps_action_driven_header_and_preview_body_after_shell_adoption",
      "severity": "S2",
      "description": "After the retrofit the Landing Preview page must still render its preview body and preserved root test id, still gate its header on the shared action model (edit offered on DRAFT, withheld on PUBLISHED), and present the same shell navigation the overview page presents for the same event and actor. Catches a retrofit that drops preview behaviour other pages/tests depend on, or that leaves the two pages on divergent headers."
    }
  ]
}

